1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,587
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:05,213 --> 00:00:06,673
[gunshots]

3
00:00:06,756 --> 00:00:07,966
[gun clicks, fires]

4
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:10,677
[whoosh, slashing sounds]

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,679
[machine gun fire]

6
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,681
[machine gun fire continues]

7
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,765
[single gunshot]

8
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,853
[rapid gunfire]

9
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:22,397
[echoing blast]

10
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,107
[rapid gunfire]

11
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:25,942
[blade whooshing]

12
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:28,445
[tense music builds]

13
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,696
[blade whooshing]

14
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,784
[Lily] <i>He's gone. Diego's gone.</i>

15
00:00:34,868 --> 00:00:38,997
[Diego] <i>Even though I've left this world,</i>
<i>I'll always be in your heart.</i>

16
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,415
<i>I'll watch over you.</i>

17
00:00:40,498 --> 00:00:41,708
[voice breaking] <i>Diego.</i>

18
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,169
[reporter on TV] <i>The shocking video</i>

19
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,171
<i>of Lily Cruz's public torture</i>
<i>has finally been released.</i>

20
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,797
<i>We will hunt you down!</i>

21
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:51,301
[Julio] <i>Is this the punishment</i>
<i>you're giving me?!</i>

22
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,386
<i>I am Julio Ardiente!</i>

23
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:55,096
<i>And whoever you send to punish me,</i>

24
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,682
<i>I'll send them back to you</i>
<i>with a bullet in their head!</i>

25
00:00:57,766 --> 00:00:59,976
<i>Do you hear me?! Punish me if you want!</i>

26
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,520
[Lily] <i>I'm not the only one who loves you.</i>

27
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,773
<i>The people do as well.</i>

28
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:09,027
<i>And I promise to love this province</i>

29
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:13,114
<i>the way you loved the people of Ardiente.</i>

30
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:15,742
<i>Goodbye, Diego. I love you so much.</i>

31
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:20,246
[Julio] <i>Emilia is nothing</i>
<i>but a stupid weakling.</i>

32
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:24,292
<i>She takes after her mother.</i>
<i>They're both stupid!</i>

33
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:32,342
<i>I am the fire that engulfed</i>
<i>your precious Red Dragon.</i>

34
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:37,472
<i>I killed Red Dragon.</i>

35
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:39,808
[screaming]

36
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:41,768
[Camia] <i>Lily, don't be like the people</i>

37
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:42,769
<i>who killed Diego.</i>

38
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:45,396
<i>No matter how grave their crime was,</i>

39
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,149
<i>that doesn't give you</i>
<i>the right to take their lives.</i>

40
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:51,069
[Lily] <i>Not even their deaths</i>
<i>would be punishment enough</i>

41
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:52,946
<i>for what they did to Diego.</i>

42
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:57,909
-[gunshots]
-[suspenseful music playing]

43
00:01:57,992 --> 00:02:01,079
You, go there. Follow me. Move.

44
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:02,539
Go, go, go!

45
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:06,209
[gunshots]

46
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:09,254
[water splashing]

47
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,884
-[exclaims]
-[glass shatters]

48
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:19,013
[whimpering, breathing heavily]

49
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:22,809
-[grunts]
-[cocks gun]

50
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:28,273
Papa, you monster. You monster.

51
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:36,114
You're heartless. I hate you. I hate you!

52
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:38,241
[suspenseful music playing]

53
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:40,660
[gunshots]

54
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:50,670
[gunshots]

55
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:05,602
-[suspenseful music intensifies]
-[gunshots]

56
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:12,901
[Natalie yelping]

57
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:22,744
[thuds]

58
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,831
[grunting]

59
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:30,293
[yelps]

60
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:32,128
[suspenseful music playing]

61
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:36,883
[gunshot]

62
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,844
[gunshots]

63
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,683
[grunting]

64
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:48,686
Men, follow Lily!

65
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:49,896
Let's go!

66
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:53,942
You, secure the area! Arrest all of them!

67
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:56,611
[suspenseful music intensifies]

68
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:09,791
-[gunshot]
-[bullet ricochets]

69
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:11,417
[crying]

70
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:16,464
Papa! Papa!

71
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:21,886
[suspenseful sting]

72
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,853
[breathing shakily]

73
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:36,776
[suspenseful sting]

74
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:45,368
I suppose you already know
the truth, Emilia.

75
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:51,958
You already know that it was
your father who killed Helena.

76
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:53,960
Your mother.

77
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:55,670
[breathing heavily]

78
00:04:55,753 --> 00:04:58,965
What are you doing here? Why are you here?

79
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:06,514
-Here.
-[paper rustles]

80
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:09,976
-Read that. Everything's there.
-[suspenseful music playing]

81
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:13,563
That's proof that it was your father

82
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:15,815
who killed your loved ones.

83
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,692
[suspenseful music playing]

84
00:05:17,775 --> 00:05:21,571
Your Aunt Claire, your mother,

85
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:25,783
and even your son, Arnaldo.

86
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:28,536
[crying]

87
00:05:28,619 --> 00:05:30,621
It's all in there. Read it!

88
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:35,001
That document proves
that I didn't kill Arnaldo!

89
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:39,297
I didn't have him killed.
Your son committed suicide!

90
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:43,509
He killed himself because of all the lies

91
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,928
that your father told him!

92
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:48,097
[suspenseful music playing]

93
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:51,100
Let me ask you, Emilia.

94
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:55,646
Would you rather live a lie…

95
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:59,567
than face the truth?

96
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:00,651
[sniffles]

97
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:02,862
-Stop it.
-The truth

98
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:05,114
is right in front of you, Emilia.

99
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:08,201
All you need to do is wake up!

100
00:06:08,701 --> 00:06:11,204
[suspenseful music playing]

101
00:06:16,125 --> 00:06:17,543
Your father lied to you.

102
00:06:18,961 --> 00:06:20,963
He blamed all his crimes,

103
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:26,052
everything he did, on us, to fool you!

104
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:30,765
You ruined my life

105
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:33,101
and the lives of so many people.

106
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:37,355
You did all that just to prove
yourself to him.

107
00:06:39,982 --> 00:06:44,195
[Julio] <i>This is all your fault.</i>

108
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:49,826
<i>You. You and your weaknesses as a woman!</i>

109
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:52,537
<i>-You never think, do you?</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

110
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:54,163
<i>A woman like you,</i>

111
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,790
<i>getting herself drunk senseless?!</i>

112
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,291
-<i>Show some dignity!</i>
-[exclaims, sobs]

113
00:06:57,375 --> 00:07:03,464
[Julio] <i>I will treat you the way</i>
<i>you deserve to be treated.</i>

114
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:05,466
<i>And until now,</i>

115
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:09,971
<i>I still see you as a weak woman.</i>

116
00:07:10,054 --> 00:07:12,974
[Emilia] <i>All my life,</i>
<i>you've been doing this to me!</i>

117
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:15,476
<i>Why is it so difficult</i>
<i>for you to save me?!</i>

118
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,729
<i>Why is it so difficult</i>
<i>for you to love me, Papa?!</i>

119
00:07:18,813 --> 00:07:23,651
[Julio] <i>Emilia is nothing</i>
<i>but a stupid weakling!</i>

120
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:29,031
<i>I killed Red Dragon.</i>

121
00:07:30,741 --> 00:07:32,660
You were just a pawn
in your father's game.

122
00:07:33,369 --> 00:07:35,079
All your life, you loved him,

123
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:37,206
all your life, he's made you a fool!

124
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:40,668
All your life, you've been
trying to prove yourself!

125
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,213
But your father will never love you

126
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:47,383
because the only person
he loves is himself.

127
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:50,303
[sobbing] That's enough.

128
00:07:50,803 --> 00:07:53,347
-Stop.
-That's the truth, Emilia.

129
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:58,478
That's the truth, so accept it.
Your father will never love you.

130
00:07:58,561 --> 00:08:01,355
All the wealth you acquire means nothing

131
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:04,984
because your father loves
no one else but himself!

132
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:11,199
Enough! Stop it. Just stop!

133
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:13,493
[whimpering]

134
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,996
Everything you saw,

135
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:21,542
I planned all that, Emilia!

136
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,629
So you'll know the truth!

137
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:29,675
<i>The name Stefano dela Torre came up too.</i>

138
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:31,719
<i>Does it sound familiar?</i>

139
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:35,473
<i>The legendary Lily Cruz.</i>

140
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:39,519
<i>What have I done right</i>
<i>to deserve such a visit?</i>

141
00:08:39,977 --> 00:08:40,978
<i>Please, have a seat.</i>

142
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:46,400
<i>I guess the rumors about you are true.</i>

143
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:50,988
<i>You are brave, very much so.</i>

144
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,156
[laughs]

145
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,701
<i>What's this?</i>

146
00:08:57,036 --> 00:09:02,750
<i>In your hands is proof that Julio Ardiente</i>

147
00:09:02,833 --> 00:09:05,169
<i>killed Red Dragon.</i>

148
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:10,466
<i>I only wanted to inform you</i>

149
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:17,014
<i>that you have a couple</i>
<i>of snakes in your backyard.</i>

150
00:09:17,098 --> 00:09:21,185
<i>I already know</i>
<i>how cunning Julio Ardiente is.</i>

151
00:09:22,103 --> 00:09:25,481
<i>But I never thought he was arrogant enough</i>

152
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,067
<i>to bite the hand of a god.</i>

153
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,528
-[tense music playing]
-[laughing]

154
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:36,993
<i>Well, Julio Ardiente</i>
<i>doesn't believe in gods.</i>

155
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:44,709
<i>Don't you think Emilia should find out</i>

156
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:47,378
<i>what happened to her mother?</i>

157
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:49,422
<i>Your…</i>

158
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:52,967
<i>Red Dragon.</i>

159
00:09:53,801 --> 00:09:55,303
<i>And what makes you think…</i>

160
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,889
<i>that we will cooperate with you?</i>

161
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:04,687
[tense music playing]

162
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:07,523
<i>What's the plan?</i>

163
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:10,484
<i>I'll have to take a shower.</i>

164
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:11,569
<i>I'll be waiting here.</i>

165
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:14,864
[door closes]

166
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:17,158
[tense music playing]

167
00:10:26,584 --> 00:10:31,964
Your beloved father, the one
you thought loved you back,

168
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:35,968
will be the one to drag you to hell!

169
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,387
[whimpering]

170
00:10:41,349 --> 00:10:42,475
Shut up!

171
00:10:42,558 --> 00:10:45,144
Your father is just using you.
He's just using you.

172
00:10:45,227 --> 00:10:47,563
He doesn't love you. No one loves you.

173
00:10:47,647 --> 00:10:49,398
He's just using you!

174
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:51,484
-He never loved you!
-[shushes]

175
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:55,154
Open your eyes, and stop being his puppet!

176
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:56,739
[shushes, sobs]

177
00:10:56,822 --> 00:10:57,990
Shut up!

178
00:10:58,282 --> 00:11:00,618
Wake up, Emilia!

179
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:04,872
Your father will never love you!

180
00:11:05,956 --> 00:11:10,878
One day, the father you love
so much will kill you

181
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:13,631
because he never loved you back!

182
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:19,387
Stop! I'm sick and tired of this!

183
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:23,891
Whether you're Ivy Aguas or Lily Cruz,

184
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:27,061
if you want payback, then just do it!

185
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:30,523
I'm sick and tired of this!
I've had enough!

186
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:31,857
[gunshots]

187
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:34,235
Stop it! Shut up!

188
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:36,946
[groans] Papa!

189
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:43,953
[suspenseful music playing]

190
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:46,497
-Papa!
-[gunshots]

191
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,582
[Julio] Kill that woman!

192
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:53,170
-[gunshot]
-[Emilia grunts]

193
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:55,339
[rapid gunfire]

194
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,635
[gunshots]

195
00:12:00,136 --> 00:12:02,430
[suspenseful music playing]

196
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:06,934
[Lily] Where do you think
you're going, Julio Ardiente?!

197
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:17,111
[Julio] Just as I thought.
I had a nagging feeling

198
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:20,614
that you were the reason behind this mess.

199
00:12:21,115 --> 00:12:24,243
The immortal Lily Cruz.

200
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:26,620
I've waited so long for this moment.

201
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:29,623
To finally come face to face
with my husband's killer.

202
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:33,502
Diego's life is the last one
you'll ever take.

203
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:36,672
My life is the last one you'll ever ruin.

204
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:39,341
I won't let you ruin any more lives!

205
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,094
Go ahead, if you want to be a hero.

206
00:12:43,304 --> 00:12:46,640
It's all yours. But be ready to die.

207
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,978
Because everyone I knew
who played the hero

208
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:53,022
ended up dead.

209
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:58,944
When you killed my husband,
you already took my life, Julio.

210
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:02,072
That's why I'm not afraid to die!

211
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:05,701
I've always known
that you aren't afraid to die.

212
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:09,997
But the question is,
are you willing to kill?

213
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:12,917
[suspenseful music playing]

214
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,094
[Diego] <i>Violence isn't the answer to evil.</i>

215
00:13:24,845 --> 00:13:28,974
<i>We only use guns to protect ourselves.</i>

216
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:31,393
<i>Wake up! We have to fight back.</i>

217
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:33,062
-[Diego] <i>Fine, be a killer.</i>
-[Jepoy] <i>Now's the time!</i>

218
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:35,147
<i>Fine, go ahead and kill. Let's all kill!</i>

219
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,191
<i>How will that make us</i>
<i>any different from them?!</i>

220
00:13:37,274 --> 00:13:38,317
[suspenseful sting]

221
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,737
[emotive female vocal music playing]

222
00:13:43,405 --> 00:13:44,615
[screams]

223
00:13:44,698 --> 00:13:46,867
[breathing heavily]

224
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:48,619
[Julio] You see?

225
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:54,041
You see? This is your problem, Lily Cruz,

226
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:59,213
and everyone else who would like
to be a hero like you.

227
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:02,049
You want to be a hero.

228
00:14:02,466 --> 00:14:03,509
[chuckles]

229
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:09,139
I know you've always wanted to kill me

230
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:11,684
for as far back as I can remember.

231
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:13,811
But you know what?

232
00:14:16,188 --> 00:14:19,024
You have an immaculate heart.

233
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:25,990
That's why you can't stain
your hands with blood.

234
00:14:27,616 --> 00:14:32,454
Just like how you don't want
to stain with blood

235
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:36,083
your husband's memory.

236
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,210
That is why…

237
00:14:40,296 --> 00:14:46,427
Diego is dead, and I am still alive!

238
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:49,722
Aside from that…

239
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:53,434
you're a woman.

240
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,146
No matter how intelligent
you are, or how good you are,

241
00:14:58,772 --> 00:15:01,984
you always let your heart get in the way.

242
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:07,948
And that, my dear,
is your greatest weakness.

243
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:10,576
You're just a woman.

244
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,830
I always let my heart lead me

245
00:15:15,539 --> 00:15:18,417
because I know that in every battle,

246
00:15:18,792 --> 00:15:20,377
love will always prevail.

247
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:25,549
I'm surrounded by people
who love me, Julio.

248
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:32,306
But you? Does anybody love you?
And yes, I am a woman.

249
00:15:32,389 --> 00:15:36,727
But let me ask you, who was it
that brought you down?

250
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,939
Wasn't it a woman?!

251
00:15:40,397 --> 00:15:43,025
And now, she's right in front of you!

252
00:15:43,317 --> 00:15:45,903
I brought you down!

253
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:47,821
-[chuckles]
-[Lily] A woman

254
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:52,159
brought old man Julio Ardiente down!

255
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:53,118
And that's me!

256
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:57,456
What a woman thing to say!

257
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:59,541
[laughing]

258
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,001
[gunshot]

259
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:06,298
Would you call that
a "woman thing" to do, Papa?!

260
00:16:07,091 --> 00:16:09,426
[suspenseful music playing]

261
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:14,056
[sniffles]

262
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:27,069
I am no hero, that's why I can kill you!

263
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:32,157
You idiot! You never can,
and you never will!

264
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:33,450
[dramatic music playing]

265
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:35,953
You're just like Lily Cruz.

266
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:41,250
You're a woman! You are weak! Weak!

267
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:44,920
You killed my mother.

268
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,049
You ruined my son's life.

269
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:54,096
I even killed my own husband for you.

270
00:16:55,389 --> 00:17:00,269
You also killed Aunt Claire,
the only person who loved me!

271
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:04,565
When all I wanted from you
was for you to love

272
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:06,650
and respect me, at least!

273
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,944
But you never did!

274
00:17:10,446 --> 00:17:12,364
[suspenseful music playing]

275
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:15,659
What did you say?

276
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:18,787
I'm weak because I'm just
a woman like Lily Cruz?!

277
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:29,423
I despise you more than Lily Cruz!

278
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:32,301
[suspenseful music playing]

279
00:17:35,763 --> 00:17:37,765
If she can't kill you…

280
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,351
then I will!

281
00:17:41,435 --> 00:17:43,562
[suspenseful music intensifies]

282
00:17:47,816 --> 00:17:50,152
[gunshots]

283
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:54,531
Lily! Lily!

284
00:17:55,574 --> 00:17:57,159
-[gunshot]
-[exclaims]

285
00:17:57,534 --> 00:17:59,536
[suspenseful music playing]

286
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:01,705
[Julio groans]

287
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:08,921
[gunshot]

288
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:10,214
[groans]

289
00:18:13,175 --> 00:18:15,803
[suspenseful music intensifies]

290
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:19,139
[screaming]

291
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:21,725
[gunshot]

292
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,354
[gunshot]

293
00:18:26,438 --> 00:18:29,274
-[screaming]
-[gunshots]

294
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,363
[sobbing]

295
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:39,409
[emotive vocal choir music playing]

296
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:44,623
[Lily] <i>I'll take you all down.</i>

297
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:46,291
-[screams]
-[gunshot]

298
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:58,554
[dramatic music playing]

299
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:01,390
[Lily] <i>I'll take you all down one by one</i>

300
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:06,436
<i>until you beg me</i>
<i>to just end your suffering.</i>

301
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,772
[dramatic music playing]

302
00:19:08,856 --> 00:19:10,774
[Emilia sobbing]

303
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:26,165
Lily, please. Kill me, please.

304
00:19:26,248 --> 00:19:28,333
I'm begging you.

305
00:19:29,084 --> 00:19:33,005
Kill me now, please. [sniffles]

306
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:35,507
[suspenseful music playing]

307
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:37,634
Please.

308
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:41,138
-No.
-Kill me, I'm begging you.

309
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:46,852
Lily, please.

310
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:50,063
Lily.

311
00:19:51,064 --> 00:19:58,071
Lily, I beg you.
I don't have anything left.

312
00:20:03,076 --> 00:20:06,580
Kill me, please.

313
00:20:08,373 --> 00:20:13,712
I beg you. Please kill me.

314
00:20:14,087 --> 00:20:15,172
[sobbing]

315
00:20:17,674 --> 00:20:20,219
[Lily] <i>I shouldn't stain</i>
<i>my hands with blood.</i>

316
00:20:25,515 --> 00:20:28,435
<i>Justice, not revenge.</i>

317
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,938
<i>Just like what Miss Prianka taught me.</i>

318
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:34,149
[Emilia sobbing]

319
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,692
[straining] Lily…

320
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:42,532
[echoing] Please…

321
00:20:58,465 --> 00:21:01,009
[dramatic music playing]

322
00:21:13,814 --> 00:21:14,856
[suspenseful sting]

323
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:20,028
[Natalie] Yay!

324
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:21,571
[chuckles]

325
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:24,616
[dramatic tense music playing]

326
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:32,708
Lily, Emilia was brought to the hospital.

327
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:37,170
The bullet hit her spine.
She's definitely paralyzed.

328
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:40,966
Thank you.

329
00:21:59,693 --> 00:22:02,029
[dramatic tense music playing]

330
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:09,536
[Lily] <i>You'll finally get</i>
<i>what you deserve.</i>

331
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:15,167
[music stops]

332
00:22:21,423 --> 00:22:23,008
[footsteps approaching]

333
00:22:24,259 --> 00:22:25,385
-Mom.
-[Camia] Lily.

334
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:29,014
[dramatic triumphant music playing]

335
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:30,599
Jepoy.

336
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:48,325
Jepoy, I don't know
what I'd do if I lost you.

337
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:51,536
I didn't let anything harm me
because of you, Anna.

338
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:54,998
[dramatic triumphant music playing]

339
00:23:00,837 --> 00:23:02,714
-Natalie…
-[shushes]

340
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:06,176
It's okay. I get it.

341
00:23:06,259 --> 00:23:08,553
Like, you don't have to say anything.

342
00:23:09,387 --> 00:23:12,390
You know what? You've saved me,
and you've done so much.

343
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:14,935
And I just want to let you go

344
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:17,479
wherever you're happy,
and you two look really happy.

345
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,773
You look like you're gonna have
a lot of kids and stuff.

346
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:25,862
Um, I'll find happiness
someday soon perhaps.

347
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:34,621
Lily. Are the Ardientes really gone?

348
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:40,210
It's all over.

349
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:43,088
The Ardientes are gone.

350
00:23:44,381 --> 00:23:46,007
We can finally live in peace.

351
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:49,594
And the people of Ardiente can start anew.

352
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:54,641
[dramatic triumphant music playing]

353
00:24:09,739 --> 00:24:12,868
[lively music playing]

354
00:24:23,336 --> 00:24:25,380
WELCOME TO POBLACION ARDIENTE

355
00:24:30,677 --> 00:24:32,637
[children talking, giggling]

356
00:24:32,721 --> 00:24:38,518
-[feel-good music playing]
-[kids shouting, laughing]

357
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,770
Lily, Ma'am Georgina,

358
00:24:40,854 --> 00:24:44,065
thank you so much
for visiting the orphanage.

359
00:24:45,775 --> 00:24:49,196
Kids, let's say good morning
to Lily Cruz-Torillo.

360
00:24:50,363 --> 00:24:52,616
[kids and Jepoy] Good morning!

361
00:24:53,575 --> 00:24:55,327
Good morning, kids.

362
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:56,953
Before you continue,

363
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:58,997
I've brought with me today Atty. Fisher.

364
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:01,374
Can you say good morning to her too?

365
00:25:01,458 --> 00:25:03,752
[kids and Jepoy] Good morning!

366
00:25:03,835 --> 00:25:05,837
Good morning! [chuckles]

367
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:08,298
Okay. You can continue playing now.

368
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:12,636
It's important that I see
for myself how you are doing,

369
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:15,931
so I can see how the Aguas Foundation
can help even more.

370
00:25:17,515 --> 00:25:19,267
I see you're just like Lily.

371
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,852
You're compassionate too.

372
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:22,604
-Right, Anna?
-Jepoy.

373
00:25:22,687 --> 00:25:24,689
That's why I had no doubts

374
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:29,527
about making her the CEO of Aguas Realty.

375
00:25:29,611 --> 00:25:31,238
Not only is she smart,

376
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,990
but she also has a huge heart.

377
00:25:34,824 --> 00:25:36,826
You've put a lot of trust in me, Lily.

378
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:38,286
I don't want to break it.

379
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:40,080
Now, I have to leave.

380
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:42,123
I'm needed in our Manila office.

381
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:43,416
Thank you, Attorney.

382
00:25:44,167 --> 00:25:45,085
-I'll get going.
-Thank you.

383
00:25:45,168 --> 00:25:46,962
-Thank you, Attorney.
-[Anna] Take care.

384
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,214
[soft piano music playing]

385
00:25:49,297 --> 00:25:51,675
[kids chatting, shouting]

386
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:55,887
Look.

387
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:00,892
[soft piano music playing]

388
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:19,494
[Jepoy] You guys saw that?

389
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:28,044
I'm sure Nanny Carlotta's
happy for us now.

390
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:35,510
Same here, Jepoy. Ever since we were kids,

391
00:26:36,011 --> 00:26:39,973
all she ever wanted
was for us to be happy.

392
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,392
That's why, like her,

393
00:26:44,019 --> 00:26:46,146
I'm happy for both of you too.

394
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:47,897
[chuckles]

395
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:52,944
[chuckles]

396
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:55,447
[Jepoy and Anna chuckling]

397
00:26:56,948 --> 00:26:58,783
Good morning, Lily Cruz-Torillo.

398
00:26:59,409 --> 00:27:00,285
[smooches]

399
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:03,246
You are now officially late
for your next appointment

400
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:06,041
with your BFF. Me. [laughs]

401
00:27:06,124 --> 00:27:08,168
So what now, girl?

402
00:27:08,251 --> 00:27:12,130
Oh, well, I have to go because
my assistant here is in a hurry.

403
00:27:12,213 --> 00:27:14,466
-Assistant? Me?
-Just kidding.

404
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:16,343
-You're cooking, right?
-Yes.

405
00:27:16,426 --> 00:27:18,928
Lily, Natalie, have dinner with us.

406
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,680
Anna's cooking. She's really good.

407
00:27:20,889 --> 00:27:22,849
By dinner, you mean…

408
00:27:24,225 --> 00:27:26,102
I'm just kidding. I get it, dinner.

409
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:28,021
You're inviting me for dinner?

410
00:27:28,104 --> 00:27:30,190
-Just say yes.
-Hmm… Okay.

411
00:27:30,607 --> 00:27:34,778
We'll be at the dinner
with old friends. Sure.

412
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:38,865
But, of course, we have
to go to another event,

413
00:27:38,948 --> 00:27:42,202
where all my constituents
are waiting for me.

414
00:27:42,285 --> 00:27:44,704
-Yours?
-[chuckles] I'm just kidding.

415
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:46,748
<i>Your</i> constituents are waiting for me.

416
00:27:46,831 --> 00:27:47,832
I'm just kidding. You.

417
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:49,417
They're waiting for you,
of course. [chuckles]

418
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,544
-Let's go. Hurry up!
-Crazy Natalie.

419
00:27:51,628 --> 00:27:53,338
-I'll text you, okay?
-Sure.

420
00:27:53,421 --> 00:27:54,672
-Bye, Lily.
-Take care.

421
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,841
-Take care. Bye.
-Text me back.

422
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:59,260
-[Jepoy] All right. Later.
-Goodbye, kids!

423
00:27:59,969 --> 00:28:02,055
-Kids, say goodbye!
-Take care of yourselves. Enjoy!

424
00:28:02,138 --> 00:28:03,473
[kids] Bye!

425
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:09,354
Jepoy, when we were kids,

426
00:28:09,437 --> 00:28:12,065
I never knew I could be this happy.

427
00:28:13,233 --> 00:28:14,484
But I am now.

428
00:28:15,485 --> 00:28:19,948
You, me, and Lily are happy.
All because of Nanny Carlotta.

429
00:28:22,742 --> 00:28:24,369
You're my life, Anna.

430
00:28:27,330 --> 00:28:29,999
[heartwarming music playing]

431
00:28:53,314 --> 00:28:55,775
[soft sentimental music playing]

432
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:10,790
"HOPE. CHANGE. LOVE."

433
00:29:25,388 --> 00:29:27,766
-[Carlotta laughing]
-[young Lily] <i>You're it!</i>

434
00:29:28,183 --> 00:29:31,227
<i>Nanny! You're already it!</i>

435
00:29:32,437 --> 00:29:36,775
<i>You're it! Nanny! You're it!</i>

436
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:38,818
[Carlotta laughing]

437
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,114
[Carlotta] <i>Okay. I'm it!</i>

438
00:29:43,198 --> 00:29:45,742
[grunting playfully, laughing]

439
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:52,791
[soft sentimental music playing]

440
00:29:57,170 --> 00:29:59,881
[Dante] <i>Come on, Lily! Push! Harder!</i>

441
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:01,090
<i>A bit more!</i>

442
00:30:02,675 --> 00:30:03,635
[engine starts]

443
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:05,762
<i>There we go! </i>[shouts with joy]

444
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:11,226
[birds chirping]

445
00:30:20,235 --> 00:30:22,987
[soft sentimental music playing]

446
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:27,283
"HOPE. CHANGE. LOVE."

447
00:30:35,333 --> 00:30:36,334
[young Lily] <i>I'm Lily.</i>

448
00:30:38,127 --> 00:30:40,797
<i>Are you Governor Ardiente's grandson?</i>

449
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:46,970
[sentimental music playing]

450
00:31:01,651 --> 00:31:06,489
[Lily] <i>We will never forget all</i>
<i>the sacrifices you made for us.</i>

451
00:31:06,573 --> 00:31:12,287
<i>We will dedicate every sunrise</i>
<i>here in Bagong (New) Ardiente</i>

452
00:31:12,704 --> 00:31:14,706
<i>to honoring your memory.</i>

453
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:31,014
[soft piano music playing]

454
00:31:55,204 --> 00:31:56,247
[bag thuds softly]

455
00:31:57,540 --> 00:31:58,750
You waited?

456
00:32:00,376 --> 00:32:01,753
You thought I wouldn't?

457
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:05,465
I didn't expect to be pardoned.

458
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:09,594
Damian, yes, you did a lot of bad things.

459
00:32:09,969 --> 00:32:12,597
But that doesn't discount
all the good things you've done.

460
00:32:13,264 --> 00:32:15,934
You've done your time, Damian.

461
00:32:17,435 --> 00:32:18,728
You're free now.

462
00:32:21,147 --> 00:32:22,398
Yes, I'm free.

463
00:32:24,567 --> 00:32:27,236
Free to devote the rest of my days to you,

464
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,322
if you allow me to.

465
00:32:31,157 --> 00:32:34,827
Damian, I didn't wait
just to turn you down.

466
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:39,624
[romantic music playing]

467
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:09,445
[indistinct chatter]

468
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:13,783
-[applause]
-[heartwarming music playing]

469
00:33:18,413 --> 00:33:19,872
[Fernan] You've got a lot, huh?

470
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:24,252
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

471
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:26,671
[Fernan] Cheers to the newlyweds!

472
00:33:26,754 --> 00:33:28,297
[guests] Cheers!

473
00:33:28,381 --> 00:33:30,049
[glasses clinking]

474
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,968
-[man] Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!
-Kiss!

475
00:33:33,094 --> 00:33:35,054
[Fernan] There it is!

476
00:33:51,112 --> 00:33:53,781
[clears throat, whoops] Yes!

477
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:55,491
Whoo!

478
00:33:57,452 --> 00:33:59,579
[cheers and applause]

479
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:02,957
[Fernan] Look, it's the mayor!
The mayor's here!

480
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:05,293
-[man 1] Mayor!
-[man 2] Mayor!

481
00:34:06,085 --> 00:34:07,462
-Mayor.
-Miss Camia, congrats.

482
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:08,504
Thank you.

483
00:34:08,963 --> 00:34:10,006
-Congrats.
-Thank you for lending me

484
00:34:10,089 --> 00:34:11,466
-the suit.
-[laughter]

485
00:34:12,008 --> 00:34:14,886
-[Marlon] Lily.
-Mayor, thank you for coming.

486
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:18,806
Actually, someone's been waiting for you.

487
00:34:19,432 --> 00:34:20,850
Natalie's been waiting.

488
00:34:21,434 --> 00:34:23,686
-BFF, don't do this to me.
-Right?

489
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:25,104
[giggles]

490
00:34:25,688 --> 00:34:26,981
Oh. [chuckles]

491
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:29,192
Um… You know what? I'm not gonna fight it.

492
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:30,777
I think it's really written in my stars

493
00:34:30,860 --> 00:34:32,236
to end up with a mayor.

494
00:34:32,653 --> 00:34:34,447
Would you like to have a dance with me?

495
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:35,907
-Sure.
-Okay.

496
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:39,202
[Lily] Cheers to the newlyweds!

497
00:34:39,285 --> 00:34:41,829
-[glasses clinking]
-[guests] Cheers!

498
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:46,959
[heartwarming music playing]

499
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:48,503
[clinking continues]

500
00:34:48,586 --> 00:34:51,297
-[guests] Kiss! Kiss!
-[man] Fernan! Arthur!

501
00:34:52,381 --> 00:34:54,884
[guests exclaiming, whooping]

502
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:56,511
[feel-good music playing]

503
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:58,471
[no audible dialogue]

504
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,023
[Lily] <i>I wish you were here</i>
<i>to see this, Diego.</i>

505
00:35:14,862 --> 00:35:17,365
[whooping]

506
00:35:19,408 --> 00:35:20,535
[Natalie] Thank you!

507
00:35:20,618 --> 00:35:23,329
[cheers and applause]

508
00:35:24,038 --> 00:35:25,414
[Fernan] Mayor!

509
00:35:30,419 --> 00:35:31,712
[Natalie] Mayor!

510
00:35:32,839 --> 00:35:33,923
[Fernan] Mayor!

511
00:35:35,049 --> 00:35:37,218
[glasses clinking]

512
00:35:38,010 --> 00:35:39,804
Oh, Natalie.

513
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:41,389
[chuckles] She's so cute.

514
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:47,687
Lily, thank you for everything.

515
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:50,398
I just want you to be happy, Mom.

516
00:35:50,481 --> 00:35:52,191
[soft guitar music playing]

517
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:59,615
I'm sure Dad would want the same
for you, and for everyone.

518
00:36:00,741 --> 00:36:05,204
So, I'd do anything to make you happy.

519
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:12,837
But I hope you can give yourself
another chance at love

520
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:14,547
if it comes your way.

521
00:36:16,007 --> 00:36:17,091
[inhales deeply]

522
00:36:18,259 --> 00:36:20,178
I'm in no hurry, Mom.

523
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:21,804
But for now…

524
00:36:23,306 --> 00:36:25,183
I'm happy waking up each morning

525
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:28,186
feeling my husband's love.

526
00:36:28,978 --> 00:36:31,022
I'm happy waking up each morning

527
00:36:31,105 --> 00:36:33,065
with my love for him.

528
00:36:33,774 --> 00:36:36,777
Bagong Ardiente is really lucky
to have you.

529
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:40,740
This is my life now, Mom.

530
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:45,620
Bagong Ardiente is my life.

531
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:02,178
[birds chirping]

532
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:06,098
[somber music playing]

533
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:30,706
[somber music playing]

534
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:58,192
Happy birthday, Emilia.

535
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:02,905
[crying quietly]

536
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:07,660
[exhales shakily]

537
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:12,248
Why did you come here?

538
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:15,084
Just leave me alone.

539
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:19,755
You aren't alone.

540
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:27,013
Someone…

541
00:38:30,891 --> 00:38:32,310
could be waiting for you.

542
00:38:34,603 --> 00:38:36,731
It could be me…

543
00:38:41,027 --> 00:38:42,403
or anyone else.

544
00:38:45,573 --> 00:38:47,325
When you're eventually freed…

545
00:38:50,077 --> 00:38:51,746
you'll have a friend.

546
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:03,299
Why are you doing this?

547
00:39:04,842 --> 00:39:09,555
My family and I made your life
a living hell.

548
00:39:09,638 --> 00:39:11,223
The things we've done--

549
00:39:13,684 --> 00:39:14,935
Why, Lily?

550
00:39:18,606 --> 00:39:23,694
Because I believe deep down,
you're a good person.

551
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:32,286
That's why people deserve a second chance.

552
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:37,166
They deserve someone
who won't give up on them.

553
00:39:40,878 --> 00:39:42,421
It's not too late.

554
00:39:44,882 --> 00:39:47,134
You can turn your life around, Emilia.

555
00:39:55,976 --> 00:39:57,311
I'm here for you.

556
00:40:00,189 --> 00:40:02,024
[sobbing]

557
00:40:03,901 --> 00:40:04,944
Happy birthday.

558
00:40:11,617 --> 00:40:14,370
[somber music playing]

559
00:40:16,956 --> 00:40:19,250
[crowd cheering, applauding]

560
00:40:20,418 --> 00:40:23,045
Good morning, Bagong Ardiente.

561
00:40:24,922 --> 00:40:28,884
Thank you for gracing
the opening of our feast.

562
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:33,722
And now, let's hear it
for our beloved governor,

563
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,975
Governor Lily Cruz-Torillo!

564
00:40:36,058 --> 00:40:38,644
[crowd cheering, applauding]

565
00:40:45,693 --> 00:40:47,445
[crowd chanting] Bagong Ardiente!

566
00:40:47,528 --> 00:40:49,155
Bagong Ardiente!

567
00:40:49,238 --> 00:40:52,533
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

568
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:56,370
-Bagong Ardiente!
-Thank you, Bagong Ardiente.

569
00:40:56,454 --> 00:40:57,997
[chanting continues] Bagong Ardiente!

570
00:40:58,747 --> 00:41:04,295
Thank you very much for giving me a home,

571
00:41:04,962 --> 00:41:06,547
and for your unwavering trust

572
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:10,301
despite everything
that we've been through.

573
00:41:10,384 --> 00:41:13,637
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

574
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:26,484
When I first came here,
together with my parents,

575
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,070
<i>we were so hopeful</i>

576
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:33,532
<i>that this province would change our lives.</i>

577
00:41:37,244 --> 00:41:40,331
But this province changed my life…

578
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:43,542
in ways…

579
00:41:46,086 --> 00:41:47,463
that I never desired.

580
00:41:59,141 --> 00:42:05,105
But that's all behind us now.
Our dark days are finally over.

581
00:42:09,235 --> 00:42:16,325
We are all here to strengthen
Bagong Ardiente.

582
00:42:16,408 --> 00:42:20,120
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]

583
00:42:20,204 --> 00:42:23,999
[crowd cheering, applauding]

584
00:42:31,882 --> 00:42:33,175
Remember this.

585
00:42:33,968 --> 00:42:37,888
No one will ever be above the law.

586
00:42:37,972 --> 00:42:43,769
No one can dictate the course
of our lives except ourselves.

587
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:51,735
True change is not handed to us
on a silver platter.

588
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:56,865
Why should we wait for someone
to deliver the change

589
00:42:56,949 --> 00:43:00,828
if we can ignite
that change within ourselves?

590
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:07,501
We should be the change that we yearn for.

591
00:43:07,918 --> 00:43:11,589
We should embody both order and progress.

592
00:43:11,880 --> 00:43:14,508
We are the future.

593
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:24,059
So, let's all face our destinies
with courage, passion,

594
00:43:24,727 --> 00:43:26,979
and undying spirit.

595
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:33,193
Long live Bagong Ardiente!

596
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:36,280
-[all] Long live!
-Long live Bagong Ardiente!

597
00:43:36,363 --> 00:43:37,990
[all] Long live!

598
00:43:38,073 --> 00:43:39,533
[crowd chanting] Bagong Ardiente!

599
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:42,870
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

600
00:43:42,953 --> 00:43:46,415
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

601
00:43:46,498 --> 00:43:50,044
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

602
00:43:50,127 --> 00:43:53,464
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

603
00:43:53,547 --> 00:43:56,884
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

604
00:43:56,967 --> 00:44:00,429
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

605
00:44:00,512 --> 00:44:03,974
Bagong Ardiente! Bagong Ardiente!

606
00:44:04,058 --> 00:44:05,851
Bagong Ardiente!

607
00:44:06,935 --> 00:44:09,897
[Lily] <i>I hope you're seeing</i>
<i>all this, Diego.</i>

608
00:44:12,858 --> 00:44:15,277
<i>♪ She's faced the hardest times ♪</i>

609
00:44:15,361 --> 00:44:17,821
<i>♪ You can imagine ♪</i>

610
00:44:18,572 --> 00:44:25,371
<i>♪ And many times her eyes</i>
<i>Fought back the tears ♪</i>

611
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:32,252
<i>♪ And when her youthful world</i>
<i>Was about to fall in ♪</i>

612
00:44:32,586 --> 00:44:35,923
<i>♪ Each time her slender shoulders ♪</i>

613
00:44:36,006 --> 00:44:39,551
<i>♪ Bore the weight of all her fears ♪</i>

614
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:42,888
<i>♪ And a sorrow no one hears ♪</i>

615
00:44:42,971 --> 00:44:46,517
<i>♪ Still rings in midnight silence ♪</i>

616
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:49,978
<i>♪ In her ears ♪</i>

617
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:56,276
<i>♪ Let her cry for she's a lady ♪</i>

618
00:44:56,985 --> 00:45:03,867
<i>♪ Let her dream for she's a child ♪</i>

619
00:45:04,243 --> 00:45:07,788
[Lily] <i>I can't say</i>
<i>that I'm a perfect woman.</i>

620
00:45:08,747 --> 00:45:12,042
<i>My desire for revenge drove my spirit</i>

621
00:45:12,126 --> 00:45:15,003
<i>to the darkest pits of despair.</i>

622
00:45:15,087 --> 00:45:16,797
WELCOME TO BAGONG ARDIENTE

623
00:45:18,424 --> 00:45:22,594
<i>However, what guided me back</i>
<i>into the light was the love</i>

624
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:25,013
<i>I also had inside my heart.</i>

625
00:45:26,765 --> 00:45:28,517
<i>This wasn't just for me.</i>

626
00:45:29,184 --> 00:45:31,353
<i>It was for the whole province.</i>

627
00:45:32,396 --> 00:45:39,319
<i>♪ Let her dream for she's a child ♪</i>

628
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:43,031
[Lily] <i>In the end,</i>
<i>it was justice that prevailed,</i>

629
00:45:43,490 --> 00:45:45,033
<i>not vengeance.</i>

630
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:48,704
<i>Not only did forgiveness triumph,</i>

631
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:50,372
<i>but so did justice.</i>

632
00:45:52,791 --> 00:45:57,838
<i>And above all,</i>
<i>I learned to forgive myself.</i>

633
00:45:58,755 --> 00:46:02,217
<i>Because if we don't learn</i>
<i>to forgive ourselves,</i>

634
00:46:02,968 --> 00:46:05,053
<i>we will never be able</i>

635
00:46:05,137 --> 00:46:09,057
<i>to embrace the bright future</i>
<i>that lies ahead of us.</i>

636
00:46:09,516 --> 00:46:16,690
<i>♪ Let the rain fall down upon her ♪</i>

637
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:20,652
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

638
00:46:20,736 --> 00:46:23,906
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

639
00:46:23,989 --> 00:46:27,326
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

640
00:46:27,701 --> 00:46:30,370
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

641
00:46:31,079 --> 00:46:34,791
<i>♪ She's a free and gentle flower ♪</i>

642
00:46:34,875 --> 00:46:42,007
<i>♪ Growing wild ♪</i>

643
00:46:52,017 --> 00:46:56,939
Your indestructible support has
filled our hearts with passion.

644
00:46:57,022 --> 00:46:58,732
Because for a year…

645
00:46:58,815 --> 00:47:00,609
You were with us when we fought…

646
00:47:00,692 --> 00:47:02,069
-When we cried.
-And laughed.

647
00:47:02,152 --> 00:47:03,987
[exaggerated laugh]

648
00:47:04,071 --> 00:47:05,614
-When we went crazy…
-When we got captivated…

649
00:47:05,697 --> 00:47:07,115
-When things got spicy…
-And stressful…

650
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:08,367
You even made us memes!

651
00:47:08,450 --> 00:47:09,910
It was a golden journey…

652
00:47:09,993 --> 00:47:11,537
That's why we give you…

653
00:47:11,620 --> 00:47:12,913
Our golden thank you.

654
00:47:12,996 --> 00:47:15,123
We are thankful to you, our wildest fans.

655
00:47:15,207 --> 00:47:17,960
-Good job!
-Don't try me!

656
00:47:18,877 --> 00:47:22,297
[voice-over] <i>Long live </i>Wildflower!

657
00:47:22,965 --> 00:47:26,969
[all] Thank you so much, everyone!

658
00:47:27,052 --> 00:47:30,514
[all] Thank you for watching!

659
00:47:30,597 --> 00:47:33,433
[cheering]
